    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381">

                <pb facs="0288" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg238"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/448</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Advisory Commission of Railway
                        Experts to Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-08-16T11:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">August 16,
                                1918, 11 a.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.35 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Emerson reports from near Irkutsk where he and men are cooperating with Czechs
                    repairing bridges blown up by enemy. He did not get west of Urals and never in
                    touch with American Ambassador.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d381-f1"/> Czechs’ east
                    front is at south end Lake Baikal, west from Orenburg, Samara, Ekaterinburg,
                    Tyumen. Please advise families <pb facs="0289" n="239" xml:id="pg239"/> Emerson,
                    Hawkins, Johnson, Haynes, Bjonerud, location party, apparently all are well.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d381-f1" n="1" xml:id="d381-f1-content">
                <p>For reports of his efforts to mediate between the Czecho-Slovaks and Bolsheviks,
                    see <ref target="frus1918Russiav02#pg_191">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ii</hi>, pp. 191</ref> and <ref target="frus1918Russiav02#pg_212"
                        >212</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
